                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Unpolished and utterly underwhelming[/h1]\n\nThe best I can say about this thing is that it [i]could be worse[/i]. \n\nThe game consists of a mere 5 levels that unlock sequentially for beating each previous level. The gameplay peaks at level 2 - where I will admit I had some fun, if only for a short while - but the missions thereafter are lackluster and void of any actual challenge (except the final level where a guard is stood atop a staircase, shotgun barrel poised to shoot the moment you poke your head up). A rather fantastic glitch occurred upon completion of the final level, wherein all levels became unavailable to play, essentially forecably uninstalling the game for me.\n\nNow, a minor gripe, but the store pages' screenshots of the game are embellished noticably, no such fancy lighting effects actually exist in game. There may be an option to change this, but I wouldn't know, seeing as I couldn't find an options menu. ESC quits levels, and I had pretty much guessed this was going to happen, and therefore put off trying out the key until I became desperate to work out a key binding. Trial and error answered my question in the end anyways: \"Q\" is the button bound to grenade throws.\n\nOverall, not a complete failure, but despite being cheap there's better free stuff out there with leagues more polish and content.\n\n2.5/10",
